Engine (engine/)
  DOSBox, by the DOSBox Team (https://www.dosbox.com), SVN r4305, as ported
  to Emscripten by Boris Gjenero as em-dosbox
  (https://github.com/dreamlayers/em-dosbox, branch em-dosbox-svn-sdl2,
  commit e1f72dd11513c9ddc6e2a9c1f08ff50581c320f7, 2023-01-06).
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 (engine/COPYING).

  This is a modified version of the program, the same build as The Elder
  Scrolls app's: frunk.store's changes for the browser are in
  engine/em-dosbox-web.patch (also tools/elderscrolls/em-dosbox-web.patch
  in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-dos.mjs
  builds it with Emscripten 4.0.10), each change marked "[frunk]". The
  complete patched source the build came from is
  engine/em-dosbox-e1f72dd-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: linked as an ES module with JSPI in place of Asyncify, so
  DOSBox's own loop and its file reads can wait for the page; it lets the
  page run through a MessageChannel message rather than a timer, and uses
  up to 90% of the CPU rather than 60%; no splash screen and no DOSBox
  hotkeys; the page can type keys and read how many frames were drawn and
  where the game has the mouse pointer; and the pointer goes where it is
  on the screen even when a game narrows the mouse's range. Built without
  em-dosbox's function-array CPU cores, which are slower in WebAssembly.

  Libraries compiled into it: Emscripten's SDL2 port (zlib license);
  Emscripten itself (MIT / University of Illinois/NCSA licenses).

Game (data/)
  Wolfenstein 3D, shareware episode (Escape from Wolfenstein), version 1.4
  (1993). Copyright 1992 id Software, published by Apogee Software, Ltd.
  data/1wolf14.zip is the shareware as Apogee released it (sha256
  cb2a2ef7ecef14152c65ff93cc3b84fbd3e8eb0c5c1de41a6fc8cdef559451a8), from
  Apogee's FTP server (ftp.3drealms.com/share/1wolf14.zip) as the Internet
  Archive saved it on 2015-11-30. Its license (VENDOR.DOC, also in the
  game's folder) encourages everyone to copy, upload and pass the program
  around without charging for it, with all of its files as released
  included without modification; the game's folder here (WOLF3D/, out of
  the zip's W3DSW14.SHR installer archive, unpacked by tools/dos/apogee.mjs)
  is every file, unchanged, cut into 1 MB blocks (data/<version>/) for
  downloading, which the page joins back into the same files. frunk.store
  charges nothing for this app.

